// `std::map` — the hash map's name before tracker I9, kept ONE release as a
// deprecated alias. The type is `std::hash_map::HashMap` now: the name says how it
// keys (by `Hashable` value; it iterates in insertion order), leaves room for a
// sorted map beside it, and stops sharing a bare name with the reactive node that
// `derive` builds.
//
// `Map` IS `HashMap` — the re-export publishes a second spelling of the same item,
// so a `Map<str, i32>` and a `HashMap<str, i32>` are one type and pass for each
// other. Every use outside std warns with the steer; the module goes in the release
// after the one that deprecated it.
export [deprecated("use std::hash_map::HashMap")] import pkg::hash_map::HashMap as Map;
